# R8 rules for the release build. AGP passes every file in src/main/keepRules to R8.
#
# For more details, see
#   https://d.android.com/r/tools/r8/keep-rules

# The app is open source, so obfuscation hides nothing; keeping names makes users'
# crash logs readable without a mapping file. Shrinking and optimization stay on.
-dontobfuscate

# gomobile classes. The native Go library (libgojni.so) finds go.Seq and its callbacks
# by name through JNI, and Ttlvpn.start/stop are native methods bound by their JNI
# symbol names. Removing or changing them crashes the engine on load, in release only.
# The engine AAR ships these same rules as consumer rules; they are repeated here so the
# release build stays safe even if a future gomobile stops shipping them.
-keep class go.** { *; }
-keep class ttlvpn.** { *; }

# Nothing else is needed: the manifest components (activity, application, VPN service,
# tile service, widget receivers) are kept by rules AAPT2 generates from the manifest, and
# Compose, DataStore and coroutines ship their own consumer rules.
